From 3952d9ab11ea00c355c60781f1cd2f63549c6bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Downstream Patch Queue <downstream@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:19:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] Prefer the service relay for the price table

The relay publishes the repository table merged with models.dev fills, so
clients pick up newer rates without waiting for a release.

macOS, Windows and the Linux GUI try
https://agent-speed.yooztech.com/v1/prices/current first and keep the GitHub
raw file and jsDelivr as ordered fallbacks. The relay host joins each feature's
allowlist, and Settings' view-source link still points at GitHub. Every
download still goes through the existing native validator and version, date
and downgrade rules, so a relay table must prove itself like any other.

The relay table intentionally omits the table's own `tests`, so validation
rule 4 is vacuous for it; the validators already treat a missing `tests` key
as an empty list and new tests pin that. Other new tests pin the URL order and
host set, host rejection outside the allowlist, and the existing no-downgrade
and stale-date refusals along the new first source.

spec/NETWORK.md records the new order, the relay's caching and conditional-
request behaviour, and the weaker guarantee of a table without self-tests;
the privacy summaries name the relay as the first source.
